From: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
Subject: mtd: spi-nor: spansion: add SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK for s25fl064k (W25Q64)

The Winbond W25Q64 (JEDEC 0xef 0x40 0x17) on the Tenda AC10 V5 matches
the spansion s25fl064k entry in the spi-nor ID table. These chips ship
with BP=7 (whole-chip protected) + SRWD=1 set in the status register.

On Linux 6.12, spi_nor_try_unlock_all() (swp.c) only clears the block
protect bits when BOTH CONFIG_MTD_SPI_NOR_SWP_DISABLE is set AND the
flash entry carries the SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK flag. The s25fl064k entry has
no .flags, so the unlock returned early and BP stayed 7, causing every
erase/program operation to silently no-op while reads continued to
work. As a result sysupgrade could not actually write to the flash.

Add SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK | SPI_NOR_HAS_TB to the s25fl064k entry so
try_unlock_all() runs and clears BP at boot (the 3-bit default mask
covers the set BP0-2 bits; full-unlock also clears SRWD).

Signed-off-by: Naresh Solanki <naresh.solanki.2011@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/spansion.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/spi-nor/spansion.c
@@ -1036,6 +1036,7 @@
 		.id = SNOR_ID(0xef, 0x40, 0x17),
 		.name = "s25fl064k",
 		.size = SZ_8M,
+		.flags = SPI_NOR_HAS_LOCK | SPI_NOR_HAS_TB,
 		.no_sfdp_flags = SECT_4K | SPI_NOR_DUAL_READ | SPI_NOR_QUAD_READ,
 	}
 };